; A plain group referenced through a TRANSPARENT ALIAS as a homogeneous-array ELEMENT is SUPPORTED
; at both the rule-level spelling (`a = [* kv_alias]`) and the member-position one
; (`t = [ x: [* kv_alias] ]`), and generates exactly what the direct `kv` reference generates.
; This fixture records `ok`, and its class is the worse half of the alias gap: the rule-level
; spelling used to exit 0 having emitted `pub type A = Vec<KvAlias>;` and `pub type KvAlias = Kv;`
; with NO `Kv` anywhere — a crate that fails `cargo check` with E0425, so nothing in the tool's own
; exit status revealed it. Both element sites now resolve aliases before stamping the Array rep, so
; the group is materialized and the emitted `serialization.rs` is byte-identical to the direct
; spelling's (only the alias typedef and the alias-derived field name differ).
; The neighbouring already-supported shape, an anonymous array WRAPPING the aliased group
; (`t = [ x: [kv_alias] ]`), is the `WrappedBasicGroup` arm that carried this resolution first.
kv = (a: uint, b: uint)
kv_alias = kv
a = [* kv_alias]
t = [ x: [* kv_alias] ]
u = [ y: [kv_alias] ]
